@startuml agentic-product-relationships
title Agentic Product Canonical Relationships , per CR-ES-016 §8

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Agentic Product" as AP

class "Product" as P
class "Agent" as A
class "Intent" as I
class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraint" as Con
class "Agentic Workflow" as AW
class "Outcome" as O
class "Context" as Ctx
class "Capability" as Cap
class "Service" as S
class "Value" as V

AP --|> P : specializes
AP --> A : engages (optional)
AP --> I : interprets
AP --> Auth : operates-within
AP --> Pol : governed-by
AP --> Con : constrained-by
AP --> AW : uses (optional)
AP --> O : produces
AP --> Ctx : adapts-to
AP --> Cap : supports (optional)
AP --> S : delivered-through (optional)
AP --> V : contributes-to

note bottom of AP
  No foundational concept silently introduced per CR-ES-016 §8.
  Deferred concepts per ADR-ES-016 §19.
end note

@enduml
